# 🩺 CKD Prediction Web App

A Machine Learning-based web application that predicts the possibility of **Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD)** based on selected clinical parameters.

The application combines **Machine Learning, Python, Flask, SQLite, and HTML/CSS/JavaScript** to provide an interactive web-based prediction system.

> ⚠️ **Disclaimer:** This project is developed for educational and demonstration purposes only. It is **not a medical diagnostic tool** and should not be used as a substitute for professional medical advice.

---

## 📌 Project Overview

The **CKD Prediction Web App** allows users to:

* Create an account and sign in
* Enter patient clinical parameters
* Predict the possibility of Chronic Kidney Disease
* Store patient information in a database
* View saved patient records
* Generate patient PDF reports
* Manage application settings

The trained Machine Learning model is integrated into a **Flask web application**.

---

## 🎯 Problem Statement

Chronic Kidney Disease can be difficult to identify at an early stage because symptoms may not always be obvious.

This project demonstrates how Machine Learning can be integrated into a web application to analyze selected clinical parameters and provide a prediction result.

The project is intended to demonstrate the complete workflow:

**Clinical Data → Data Preprocessing → Machine Learning Model → Flask Application → Prediction → Patient Record → PDF Report**

---

## 🎯 Project Objectives

### Machine Learning Objectives

* Prepare and preprocess the CKD dataset
* Select relevant clinical parameters
* Prepare input features for the ML model
* Train a Machine Learning classification model
* Save the trained model as `model.pkl`
* Load the trained model inside the Flask application
* Generate predictions from user-entered clinical data
* Verify the model input feature structure

### Web Application Objectives

* Provide a user registration system
* Provide user sign-in functionality
* Collect patient clinical information
* Send patient data to the Machine Learning model
* Display the prediction result
* Store patient records
* View patient records
* Generate PDF reports
* Provide application settings

### Database Objectives

* Use SQLite for data storage
* Use Flask-SQLAlchemy for database interaction
* Use Flask-Migrate for database migrations
* Maintain database migration files using Alembic

---

