## 📊 Dataset

The project uses the following preprocessed dataset:

```text
CKD_Preprocessed.csv
```

The Machine Learning model uses the following **12 input features**:

| No. | Parameter                     |
| --: | ----------------------------- |
|   1 | Age (yrs)                     |
|   2 | Blood Pressure (mm/Hg)        |
|   3 | Specific Gravity              |
|   4 | Albumin                       |
|   5 | Sugar                         |
|   6 | Blood Glucose Random (mgs/dL) |
|   7 | Blood Urea (mgs/dL)           |
|   8 | Serum Creatinine (mgs/dL)     |
|   9 | Hemoglobin (gms)              |
|  10 | Hypertension: yes             |
|  11 | Diabetes Mellitus: yes        |
|  12 | Anemia: yes                   |

---

## 🤖 Machine Learning Workflow

The Machine Learning workflow is:

```text
CKD Dataset
     ↓
Data Preprocessing
     ↓
Feature Selection
     ↓
Model Training
     ↓
Model Evaluation
     ↓
Save Trained Model
     ↓
model.pkl
     ↓
Flask Application
     ↓
User Input
     ↓
Prediction
```

The trained model is stored as:

```text
model.pkl
```

---

## 🔍 Model Verification

The project contains:

```text
check_model.py
```

This file is used to verify the trained model and its expected input feature structure.

